menu "miniDSP 2x4 HD Simulator"

config MINIDSP_SIM_NO_FEEDBACK_TEST_BUILD
    bool "Build reduced no-feedback test image"
    default n
    help
        Build a reduced-capability simulator image where both playback
        alternate settings omit their feedback endpoints and the capture
        streaming alt is removed. This exists only for host-side validation
        of the driver's no-feedback fractional-rate rejection path.

config MINIDSP_SIM_PLAYBACK_CHANNEL_ONLY_FU_TEST_BUILD
    bool "Build playback feature-unit channel-only test image"
    default n
    help
        Build a descriptor variant where the playback feature unit exposes
        mute and volume only on channels 1 and 2, while master channel 0
        advertises no playback controls. This exists only to validate the
        host's per-channel capability handling.

config MINIDSP_SIM_EP0_HANG_TEST_BUILD
    bool "Build control-transfer hang test image"
    default n
    help
        Same descriptors and behavior as the default image, except that the
        first GET CUR clock-valid request after boot is never answered (its
        data stage stays NAKed). 12 seconds later the simulator
        soft-disconnects for 1 second and reconnects, with the fault disarmed
        until the next reboot. This drives the host's control-timeout path:
        abandoned request, orphaned control URB on close, and its reclaim when
        the device goes away. Product string "miniDSP 2x4HD [sim ep0-hang]".

config MINIDSP_SIM_FEEDBACK_DRIFT_TEST_BUILD
    bool "Build feedback drift test image"
    default n
    help
        Same descriptors as the default image, but the explicit feedback
        reports 2 Hz above the nominal rate (about 42 ppm), like a device
        whose clock runs fast. The simulator's periodic PACKET SIZING CHECK
        then shows whether the host follows the feedback instead of sending
        the nominal rate. Product string "miniDSP 2x4HD [sim fb-drift]".

endmenu
